// Decision-complete implementation specification for RunenGPU G4C2.
// G4C2 starts only after accepted G4C1, accepted prerequisite corrections,
// and an explicitly activated child issue on exact accepted main.

PhaseImplementationSpec(
    phase_id: "PT-RUNENGPU-G4C2",
    title: "Program, Layout, and Binding Realization",
    lifecycle_state: "planned-blocked",
    implementation_authorization_status: "blocked-until-accepted-prerequisites-and-explicit-g4c2-issue",
    owner: "RunenGPU program and binding realization owner",
    source_baseline: "accepted-main-to-be-recorded-by-g4c2-issue",
    planning_issue: "dornglut/runenwerk#209",
    implementation_issue: "dornglut/runenwerk#213",
    umbrella_issue: "dornglut/runenwerk#188",
    parent_issue: "dornglut/runenwerk#167",
    blocking_predecessor: "accepted PT-RUNENGPU-G4C1 plus accepted G4C2 readiness corrections",
    successor: "PT-RUNENGPU-G4C3",

    authority_docs: [
        "AGENTS.md",
        "TESTING.md",
        "ARCHITECTURE.md",
        "engine/Cargo.toml",
        "Cargo.lock",
        "docs-site/src/content/docs/design/active/runengpu-shader-authoring-artifact-boundary.md",
        "docs-site/src/content/docs/design/active/runengpu-g4b-contracts-g4c-delivery-design.md",
        "docs-site/src/content/docs/design/active/runengpu-g4c2-presentation-surface-binding-boundary.md",
        "docs-site/src/content/docs/workspace/specs/pt-runengpu-g4b-program-interface-layout.ron",
        "docs-site/src/content/docs/workspace/specs/pt-runengpu-g4c-wgpu-realization-cutover.ron",
        "docs-site/src/content/docs/workspace/specs/pt-runengpu-g4c1-resource-realization.ron",
    ],

    goal: "Create one private context/device-generation-bound WGPU authority for canonical WGSL modules, mandatory version-matched Naga evidence, scoped WGPU acceptance, normalized observed shader-stage IO, bind-group layouts, pipeline layouts, typed bind groups, bounded authoritative registries and optional discardable caches; share one context-wide backend-health and error-attribution authority; supersede and delete the G4C1 object-reference resource bridge with one narrowly scoped pipeline-successor bridge that carries only proven residual resource terminals plus G4C2 program/layout/bind-group terminals; remove G4C2-owned creation from the separate operation loan; and avoid realizing compute/render pipelines or performing final renderer cutover.",

    dependency_direction: [
        "Accepted G4B admitted source records, entry points, resource interfaces, stage-IO comparison vocabulary, and layouts -> G4C2 private WGSL and binding realization.",
        "Accepted G4C1 opaque resources -> G4C2 runtime binding compatibility and typed bind groups.",
        "The existing engine-private direct Naga dependency parses and validates canonical WGSL for normalized evidence; the original canonical WGSL text remains the only WGPU shader source submitted for backend realization.",
        "The G4C1 resource-private device-health observer is hoisted into one WGPU-context-wide private health owner so G4C1, G4C2, current bridges/loans, and later G4C phases observe one device-fault truth rather than parallel health registries.",
        "G4C2 deletes CurrentRenderResourceBridge and replaces it with CurrentRenderPipelineBridge, which carries only the proven residual G4C1 resource terminals that G4C2 does not itself migrate.",
        "CurrentRenderDeviceQueue remains a separately classified crate-private backend-operation loan, not an object-reference bridge. G4C2 removes ShaderModule, BindGroupLayout, PipelineLayout, and BindGroup creation from it while retaining only later-phase operation classes.",
        "Accepted G4C2 program records, observed stage-IO signatures, layouts, and bind groups -> G4C3 through opaque handles and CurrentRenderPipelineBridge, which also carries only the program/layout/bind-group terminals still required by current pipeline creation and unchanged G5 encoding.",
    ],

    pinned_parser_baseline: [
        "Accepted planning base engine/Cargo.toml directly pins wgpu 27.0.1 and naga 27.0.3 with the wgsl-in feature.",
        "The G4C2 implementation issue must re-resolve exact accepted main and record cargo tree evidence for the direct Naga parser/validator version and every WGPU-internal Naga version.",
        "Proceed only when the direct evidence path is version-compatible with the pinned WGPU implementation; if Cargo resolves different incompatible Naga major/minor authorities or WGPU changes its WGSL validation baseline, stop for the smallest explicit dependency-baseline decision.",
        "Reuse the existing direct dependency when alignment is proven; do not add a second parser, reflection crate, compiler frontend, or parallel shader-source path.",
        "For the accepted Naga 27.0.3 baseline, instantiate the evidence validator with exactly naga::valid::ValidationFlags::all() and naga::valid::Capabilities::default().",
        "The Naga 27.0.3 default capability set is the initial portable source profile. Do not add a capability merely because a broader GpuCapabilityFeature is admitted: the current RunenGPU capability vocabulary does not provide a lossless one-to-one authority for Naga extension capabilities.",
        "Capabilities::all(), manual permissive supersets, and backend-feature-to-Naga guesses are forbidden as acceptance evidence.",
        "Any Naga capability beyond Capabilities::default() requires a separately accepted RunenGPU capability/profile contract with a deterministic mapping before G4C2 may enable it.",
        "Define G4C2_NAGA_VALIDATION_PROFILE_REVISION = 1 for the accepted Naga 27.0.3 + ValidationFlags::all() + Capabilities::default() + normalization/agreement behavior; increment it only when one of those compatibility semantics changes under accepted authority.",
        "Define G4C2_WGPU_REALIZATION_COMPATIBILITY_REVISION = 1 for the accepted WGPU 27.0.1 WGSL/scoped-creation lowering behavior; increment it only when backend realization compatibility semantics change under accepted authority.",
        "No public RunenGPU type exposes naga::Module, naga::valid::ModuleInfo, handles, arenas, bindings, validation flags, capabilities, errors, or source spans.",
        "Naga types remain confined to one private G4C2 WGSL-evidence module and are normalized immediately into RunenGPU-owned facts and bounded diagnostics.",
    ],

    device_health_and_error_attribution: [
        "Introduce one crate-private WgpuDeviceHealth owned by WgpuContextState and shared by exact Arc identity wherever callbacks or subordinate realization owners require access; there is never one health registry per realization phase.",
        "Move the existing G4C1 device-lost and uncaptured-error observers from ResourceRealizationState to WgpuDeviceHealth and install them exactly once when the admitted WGPU device is composed into WgpuContextState.",
        "WgpuDeviceHealth stores only one first terminal backend-fault class plus bounded backend evidence. Its private backend-neutral classes distinguish unexpected validation, out-of-memory, and internal-or-device-lost facts; public/owner-specific error categories are translated at the consuming RunenGPU boundary rather than stored as resource-specific health truth.",
        "G4C1 keeps its accepted public failure categories by translating the shared health fact; G4C2 translates the same health authority into UnexpectedBackendProgramOrBindingValidationRejection, BackendResourceExhaustion, or ContextOrDeviceUnavailableOrLost as applicable.",
        "Scoped expected validation failures caught by a G4C2 error scope do not poison WgpuDeviceHealth. Uncaptured validation, internal error, or device-loss observations follow the one shared health path; out-of-memory remains a structured operation failure and is retained as shared terminal health only when the backend reports it uncaptured through that path.",
        "Introduce one crate-private WgpuErrorAttributionGate owned by WgpuContextState because WGPU error scopes are a device error-sink stack shared by device/queue operations rather than task-local state.",
        "The gate serializes only the synchronous WGPU dispatch interval that could interact with an active error scope: push scopes -> create/dispatch -> call pop_error_scope for every pushed scope. Calling pop_error_scope removes or initiates removal of that scope before the returned future is awaited, so release the gate after every pop call has been issued and before awaiting any pop future.",
        "Every current WGPU operation path sharing the device/queue must participate in the same attribution gate while a scoped G4C2 creation can coexist: G4C1 resource backend creation acquires it around synchronous creation, G4C2 acquires it around push/create/pop dispatch, and CurrentRenderDeviceQueue holds one lexical gate guard for the lifetime of its raw operation loan. G4C3 and later phases reuse or delete this same gate as their ownership replaces current paths; they do not create a second attribution gate.",
        "CurrentRenderDeviceQueue's guard is deliberately non-reentrant. No G4C1 resource realization or G4C2 program/layout/bind-group realization may begin while that raw operation loan is live, because those realization paths acquire the same attribution authority.",
        "The gate owns error-attribution serialization only. It is not an executor, work scheduler, submission lock, registry lock, object-reference bridge, public synchronization primitive, or GPU completion authority.",
        "No std::sync mutex guard from the attribution gate is held across an await; no authoritative registry lock is held while awaiting scoped backend completion.",
    ],

    wgsl_evidence_pipeline: [
        "Parse the exact canonical WGSL bytes with the pinned direct naga::front::wgsl path; do not parse a rewritten, formatted, preprocessed, or backend-generated source variant.",
        "Validate the parsed module with exactly the accepted versioned G4C2 Naga validation profile.",
        "Normalize entry points, resource bindings, access, type/shape/cardinality, applicable layout, vertex-input, fragment-output, builtin, override, and requirement facts from the validated module and module-info structures.",
        "Run G4B's resource-interface agreement before private WGPU module publication and retain observed stage-IO signatures for G4C3.",
        "Separately submit the original canonical WGSL text through WGPU's WGSL shader-source path; do not submit naga::Module through a Naga shader-source variant and do not create a second runtime source kind.",
        "For each publishing G4C2 WGPU creation, enter WgpuErrorAttributionGate, push nested Internal, OutOfMemory, and Validation scopes, create the object, call pop_error_scope in reverse stack order for all three scopes, then release the gate and await the three returned futures before authoritative publication.",
        "Await and inspect every popped scope result. If more than one class is observed for one creation attempt, deterministic semantic precedence is Internal or observed device loss -> ContextOrDeviceUnavailableOrLost, then OutOfMemory -> BackendResourceExhaustion, then Validation -> the operation-specific validation category; retain bounded secondary evidence but return one primary structured outcome.",
        "A shader-module Validation scope error after successful direct Naga evidence and in the absence of a higher-precedence fault is ShaderValidationPathMismatch and retains bounded evidence from both paths; it is never silently resolved in favor of one validator.",
        "A layout or bind-group Validation scope error in the absence of a higher-precedence fault is UnexpectedBackendProgramOrBindingValidationRejection.",
        "No shader module, bind-group layout, pipeline layout, or bind group record is published before its scoped backend acceptance futures resolve successfully and shared WgpuDeviceHealth is re-checked.",
        "RunenGPU realization terminals that require this scoped backend proof are async. RunenGPU does not own an executor and must not call pollster::block_on, spin an event loop, or hide synchronous waiting inside the framework/backend boundary.",
        "A Runenwerk product/integration boundary may choose how to drive an async realization future for current synchronous callers; that policy is outside RunenGPU authority and cannot become bridge, cache, registry, health, attribution-gate, or backend semantics.",
        "Publish one G4C2 program realization only when direct Naga parse/validation/evidence normalization succeeds, explicit resource-interface agreement succeeds, WGPU accepts the same canonical WGSL text, and current shared device health remains available.",
        "The direct Naga parse is evidence and diagnostics machinery, not public source identity, runtime module authority, a persisted IR, or a replacement for WGPU backend creation.",
    ],

    realized_handle_contracts: [
        "Opaque Clone non-Copy handles cover realized programs/modules, bind-group layouts, pipeline layouts, and bind groups.",
        "Every handle retains GpuContextAffinity and complete admitted descriptor or request identity for typed inspection.",
        "Program handles retain normalized observed resource-interface facts and observed vertex-input/fragment-output signatures from the pinned direct Naga evidence path.",
        "Observed facts are validation evidence only and cannot create resource declarations, vertex-buffer state, or color-target policy.",
        "Handles expose no public raw WGPU object, Naga IR, backend module output, pointer, persistence identity, or wire identity.",
        "Bind-group handles retain exact layout identity and ordered realized binding values.",
    ],

    wgsl_realization_contract: [
        "Consume only canonical WGSL admitted through the accepted G4B source registry.",
        "Reject unknown, evicted-without-live-reference, foreign-owner, or source-revision-conflicting records before parser or backend creation.",
        "Run the complete WGSL evidence pipeline before publishing the private WGPU shader module realization on a registry miss.",
        "Normalize and retain observed vertex entry-point input locations/classes and fragment entry-point output locations/classes for later G4C3 pipeline compatibility.",
        "Naga IR, module-info, and backend-native outputs remain private ephemeral implementation facts and never become public identity, cache, persistence, replay, or wire formats.",
        "Deterministic parser, validator, or agreement incompatibility rejects before backend creation. Unexpected backend validation after complete admission, resource allocation exhaustion/OOM, and unavailable/lost context/device remain distinct structured outcomes; none publishes an authoritative realization or cache entry, and backend text is diagnostic only.",
    ],

    mandatory_reflection_agreement: [
        "Normalize observed entry-point names and stages, group/binding identities, stage visibility, resource classes, access, dimensions, sample/storage format facts, array cardinality, applicable host-layout facts, vertex-input locations/classes, and fragment-output locations/classes into G4B-owned vocabulary.",
        "Use the single G4B resource-interface comparison algorithm to prove observed resource facts agree with the explicit authoritative declarations; observed statically-used stages must be a subset of declared visibility, while declared visibility may be a strict accessibility superset.",
        "Reject missing, additional, renumbered, stage-mismatched, type-mismatched, visibility-mismatched, shape-mismatched, or layout-incompatible resource facts as ProgramInterfaceMismatch.",
        "Retain normalized stage-IO signatures with the program record; do not compare them to vertex buffers or color targets until G4C3 receives a complete render pipeline descriptor.",
        "Evidence may improve source-span diagnostics but may not mutate, infer, renumber, add, or remove authoritative declarations or pipeline state.",
        "ProgramInterfaceMismatch is terminal for that realization request and cannot fall back to inferred WGPU layouts.",
    ],

    observed_stage_io_contract: [
        "Observed vertex input signatures are keyed by exact vertex entry point and contain unique shader locations plus normalized scalar/vector classes.",
        "Observed fragment output signatures are keyed by exact fragment entry point and contain unique color locations plus normalized scalar/vector classes.",
        "Builtins are represented separately from user locations and cannot be mistaken for vertex attributes or color targets.",
        "Duplicate or unsupported observed locations/classes reject program realization with a structured WGSL validation error.",
        "Observed signatures are retained realization evidence and participate in the accepted record's compatibility facts; they are not required to locate an already-published record because they do not exist before first realization.",
        "Observed signatures are not public source identity, renderer semantics, persistence authority, or a replacement for explicit render pipeline state.",
    ],

    layout_realization_contract: [
        "Realize bind-group layouts only from accepted complete GpuBindGroupLayoutDescriptor values.",
        "Realize pipeline layouts only from accepted ordered unique group-layout descriptors.",
        "Do not use WGPU automatic layout inference or shader evidence as layout authority.",
        "Validate relevant admitted features, limits, dynamic-offset constraints, array cardinality, storage texture formats, and sampler/texture compatibility before backend creation.",
        "When a group contains any binding array, enforce pinned WGPU group restrictions: no buffer in that group may use a dynamic offset and no buffer in that group may be uniform.",
        "Equal complete request descriptors may reuse one authoritative layout realization within one context/generation.",
    ],

    typed_bind_group_contract: [
        "A bind-group request names one accepted realized layout and supplies ordered typed G4B runtime binding values.",
        "The accepted G4B runtime vocabulary carries GpuBufferHandle, GpuTextureViewHandle, and GpuSamplerHandle resources. G4C2 resolves those exact logical handles through the accepted G4C1 resource-realization authority before WGPU bind-group creation; there is no G4C2 inline-sampler or second resource-creation path.",
        "Buffer ranges and texture-view facts remain the accepted G4B runtime-value semantics; sampler semantics come from the referenced G4C1 GpuSamplerHandle and its accepted realized sampler record.",
        "Validate exact resource kind, usage, range, minimum size, dynamic-offset policy and alignment, texture view/format/sample/multisample facts, storage access, sampler class, array cardinality, and context/device-generation affinity before backend creation.",
        "Reject unknown, duplicate, missing, extra, foreign, stale, or incompatible values with structured binding diagnostics.",
        "Backend bind-group creation is async, scoped, transactional, and publishes no partial authoritative entry.",
        "Every current bind-group consumer that G4C2 owns uses typed G4C1 handles directly, so CurrentRenderResourceBridge is deleted before G4C2 acceptance while only separately proven residual resource terminals move into CurrentRenderPipelineBridge.",
    ],

    validation_order: [
        "Validate admitted source/request structure and exact context affinity.",
        "Reject stale device generation.",
        "Reject an unavailable or lost context/device through the one shared WgpuDeviceHealth before authoritative lookup; an accepted record never becomes usable evidence for a dead device generation merely because its request key still matches.",
        "Construct the complete pre-realization typed request key and perform authoritative registry lookup using full equality after hashing.",
        "On an exact accepted-record hit in the same healthy context/generation, return that realization without rerunning direct Naga and without creating another WGPU object.",
        "On a miss, atomically reserve one in-flight slot for the exact complete request key before any Naga/backend work. One reserver owns the realization attempt; equal concurrent requests join that reservation rather than starting parallel Naga/WGPU creation.",
        "On a program reservation, run direct Naga parse, full validation with the accepted validation profile, normalized evidence extraction, and expected G4B program-interface/entry-point agreement on the exact canonical WGSL.",
        "On a program reservation, submit the byte-identical canonical WGSL to WGPU through the shared attribution gate and scoped async backend capture and require all scopes to resolve successfully.",
        "On layout and bind-group reservations, validate complete descriptors and typed runtime values against admitted device facts and accepted interfaces. Resolve every referenced G4B logical resource handle through G4C1 before entering the G4C2 scoped backend-creation interval.",
        "Re-check WgpuDeviceHealth after scoped backend completion and immediately before publication so a concurrent device-loss fact cannot publish a newly unusable record.",
        "Publish the authoritative ready record transactionally, resolve all equal in-flight joiners to that exact Arc record, and only then release the reservation's capacity state.",
        "On terminal failure publish no authoritative record, resolve current equal in-flight joiners to the same bounded structured failure for that attempt, remove the reservation, and permit a later independent request to retry ordinarily.",
    ],

    concurrent_realization_contract: [
        "One in-flight reservation exists at most once for one complete G4C2 request key in one context/generation. It is coordination state only, not an authoritative realization, cache entry, persisted state, or public handle.",
        "The first miss reserves; equal concurrent callers wait asynchronously outside std::sync registry locks and perform no duplicate Naga parse, WGPU creation, or capacity reservation.",
        "Distinct request keys may realize concurrently. WgpuErrorAttributionGate serializes only each synchronous error-scope dispatch interval; scoped pop futures may await concurrently after their scopes have been popped and the gate released.",
        "An in-flight reservation consumes one authoritative-capacity slot while its attempt is active so concurrent distinct misses cannot oversubscribe the configured record bound.",
        "A successful attempt converts its reserved slot directly into the one ready authoritative record and wakes all current equal joiners with the same Arc record.",
        "A terminal failed attempt releases its reserved slot after recording one bounded shared attempt result for current joiners; that failure is not a persistent negative cache and a later request may retry.",
        "Dropping/cancelling the owning realization future before a terminal result publishes no record. An RAII reservation guard removes the abandoned reservation, releases its capacity slot, and wakes equal joiners to re-enter lookup/reservation; no background task or executor-owned cleanup is required.",
        "Dropping a waiter affects only that waiter. It cannot cancel the owner, remove a ready record, or strand the reservation.",
        "No consumer callback runs under a registry or attribution-gate lock, and no std::sync lock is held across an await.",
    ],

    registry_invariants: [
        "Separate private registries own program/module, bind-group-layout, pipeline-layout, bind-group, in-flight coordination, and cache-diagnostic records.",
        "Each registry instance is scoped to exactly one GpuContextId and GpuDeviceGeneration.",
        "GpuProgramBindingRealizationPolicy owns one total nonzero authoritative record bound shared by ready plus in-flight program/module, bind-group-layout, pipeline-layout, and bind-group records; no per-kind quota is implied.",
        "DEFAULT_MAX_PROGRAM_BINDING_REALIZATION_RECORDS is 16384, matching the established G4C1 default operational scale until measurement justifies a separately accepted change.",
        "Introduce GpuRealizationPolicies as the context-level composition of GpuResourceRealizationPolicy and GpuProgramBindingRealizationPolicy. GpuContext::request uses default policies; GpuContext::request_with_realization_policies accepts an explicit composition without changing adapter selection, device-admission identity, or retry identity.",
        "Migrate callers and delete request_with_resource_realization_policy rather than retaining overlapping context-construction APIs; the unified policy composition is the one explicit override path after G4C2.",
        "Before RegistryCapacityExceeded for a new distinct request, deterministically sweep every ready authoritative G4C2 record retained only by its own registry. A record retained by any live opaque handle or authoritative dependent record is live and cannot be reclaimed; active in-flight reservations are never sweep candidates.",
        "Registry reclamation removes lookup authority and may release ordinary private WGPU object ownership; it is not GPU completion evidence, does not authorize early physical-retirement semantics, and does not move G5 lifecycle ownership.",
        "Cache eviction is never authoritative-record reclamation and may not make a live handle unknown.",
        "If the total ready-plus-in-flight record bound remains full after the registry-only sweep, fail the new distinct request with RegistryCapacityExceeded; never silently evict live authority or steal an active reservation.",
        "Each program entry retains its complete pre-realization request key plus the admitted source record, direct-evidence compatibility revision, complete explicit resource interface, normalized observed resource facts, observed stage-IO signatures, WGPU acceptance fact, and bounded diagnostics/provenance.",
        "Each layout and bind-group entry retains its complete typed request key/descriptor and exact dependency identities plus bounded backend acceptance facts.",
        "Equal duplicate requests return the same realization record; changed requests do not replace accepted identities.",
        "Hash collisions cannot authorize reuse because full typed equality follows hashing.",
        "No consumer callback executes under registry locks and no async backend wait occurs while a std::sync registry lock is held.",
        "No failure or abandoned future publishes partial authority or strands capacity/in-flight state.",
    ],

    cache_key_contracts: [
        "GpuProgramRealizationRequestKey is computable before Naga/WGPU work and includes context identity, device generation, source owner/key/revision, full canonical WGSL bytes and deterministic digest, declared entry points, complete expected resource interface, admitted requirements, G4C2_NAGA_VALIDATION_PROFILE_REVISION, and G4C2_WGPU_REALIZATION_COMPATIBILITY_REVISION.",
        "Full canonical WGSL byte equality remains authoritative; the digest only accelerates lookup/diagnostics and can never authorize reuse by itself.",
        "Normalized observed resource facts, observed stage-IO signatures, and WGPU acceptance evidence belong to the realized program record; they are deliberately excluded from the pre-realization lookup key because they do not exist until a miss is realized.",
        "Bind-group-layout request keys include context affinity, complete group descriptor, relevant admitted features/limits, and internal descriptor compatibility revision.",
        "Pipeline-layout request keys include context affinity, ordered complete group-layout identities, relevant admitted features/limits, and internal descriptor compatibility revision.",
        "Bind-group request keys include context affinity, complete layout identity, ordered typed values, complete G4C1 realization identities/ranges/generations, and relevant admitted facts.",
        "Labels, filesystem paths, authoring compiler handles, source maps, raw Naga handles, renderer IDs, WGPU object addresses, backend error text, and naked hashes are excluded.",
    ],

    cache_behavior: [
        "Authoritative registry lookup uses complete pre-realization request keys. An exact live ready match in a healthy context/generation returns the accepted realization directly and records Hit without rerunning evidence/backend creation.",
        "An equal in-flight match joins the existing attempt and does not count as a second cache miss or backend realization.",
        "An absent ready/in-flight authoritative entry records Miss and follows reservation plus complete ordinary realization.",
        "Optional derived acceleration caches are in-memory, discardable, reconstructable, context/generation-scoped, and non-authoritative. A stale/incompatible derived entry records Rejected, is discarded or quarantined, and falls back to authoritative lookup/reservation/ordinary realization.",
        "A cache never bypasses affinity, generation, current context/device health, full-key equality, authoritative-record liveness, in-flight single-flight coordination, or capacity checks.",
        "Resource-interface or Naga/WGPU validation-path disagreement is a semantic rejection, not a cache miss or fallback.",
        "Unexpected backend validation, backend resource exhaustion/OOM, and unavailable/lost context/device emit distinct structured outcomes and publish no authoritative entry; RealizationFailed may aggregate telemetry but is not their semantic classification.",
        "No persisted module, layout, bind-group, Naga IR, module-info, observed signature, backend output, in-flight reservation, or cross-process handle format is authorized.",
    ],

    successor_migration_bridge: [
        "Delete CurrentRenderResourceBridge before publishing G4C2 acceptance; it has zero remaining source references and its still-required access is represented only by the successor's proven residual terminals.",
        "Permit exactly one crate-private module named CurrentRenderPipelineBridge after G4C2 acceptance.",
        "The bridge exists only because audited current pipeline-creation and unchanged G5 encoding operations still require the proven residual G4C1 resources and G4C2 program/layout/bind-group objects until G4C3 supersedes it.",
        "The bridge accepts validated opaque G4C1 resource and G4C2 program, bind-group-layout, pipeline-layout, and bind-group handles and exposes only narrowly typed owner-local terminals for exact audited current pipeline-creation and encoding consumers; it exposes no public accessor, Deref, AsRef, reusable raw handle, generic raw-WGPU callback, or arbitrary consumer closure.",
        "The bridge may lend borrowed resource, shader-module, layout, and bind-group references only for lexical use through those purpose-typed terminals; borrowed values cannot escape, be stored, cloned into ownership, cached, returned, persisted, or treated as resource/program/layout/pipeline identity.",
        "A terminal may support its unchanged later-phase operation, but the bridge never performs or owns pipeline realization, command encoding, uploads, submission, async driving, or any other operation.",
        "The bridge owns validated access only; it does not validate stage IO and owns no resource, source, interface, layout, pipeline descriptor, cache, execution, progress, completion, or lifecycle truth.",
        "Bridge lookup repeats exact context/device-generation, shared current context/device-health, and handle-kind validation and invokes no external callback under registry locks.",
        "Source guards permit exactly this named object-reference bridge and its audited current terminals and reject a second pipeline bridge, the deleted resource bridge, or broad raw-WGPU object-reference reach-through outside the separately bounded CurrentRenderDeviceQueue operation loan.",
        "G4C3 must delete CurrentRenderPipelineBridge before publishing G4C3 acceptance, migrating terminals it owns and carrying only proven residual resource/bind-group terminals plus newly realized G4C3 pipeline terminals into its single execution successor bridge.",
    ],

    current_render_device_queue_cutover: [
        "CurrentRenderDeviceQueue is a separate crate-private backend-operation loan, not CurrentRenderPipelineBridge, not a second object-reference bridge, and not a generic callback, native-interop, Deref, or AsRef API.",
        "At G4C2 acceptance, CurrentRenderDeviceQueue acquires and retains the one WgpuErrorAttributionGate lexical guard for the whole raw device/queue loan so current G4C3/G5 WGPU operations cannot enter while a G4C2 error-scope dispatch interval is active.",
        "The current source acquires CurrentRenderDeviceQueue above the broad renderer.render call. G4C2 must split this integration ordering: finish all G4C1 resource and G4C2 program/layout/bind-group realization needed by that render batch before acquiring the raw loan, then acquire the loan only for the remaining unchanged current G4C3 pipeline-creation and G5 encoding/queue operation interval.",
        "No GpuContext::realize_* G4C1 resource call and no G4C2 realization terminal may execute while CurrentRenderDeviceQueue is alive. Do not solve this with a reentrant gate, a second gate, or an ungated raw path.",
        "If the exact-current-main census finds a genuinely unavoidable G4C1/G4C2 realization that cannot be moved before raw-loan acquisition without changing G5 semantics, stop before implementation for the smallest explicit migration decision rather than weakening error attribution.",
        "At G4C2 acceptance, the loan's source-guarded exact call sites have zero ShaderModule, BindGroupLayout, PipelineLayout, or BindGroup creation operations, in addition to the G4C1 resource-creation removals.",
        "The remaining operation classes and exact call sites are monotonically shrinking G5 evidence. G4C3 removes pipeline creation; G5 migrates encoding/upload/submission/copy/map/readback users and deletes the loan. Deletion or later replacement of the attribution gate follows actual remaining WGPU operation/error-attribution needs rather than bridge lifetime.",
    ],

    current_consumer_migration: [
        "Repeat the exact-current-main census for shader-module, binding-layout, pipeline-layout, bind-group, runtime-binding, parameter-byte, sidecar, renderer setup, material, UI, example, bench, and test consumers.",
        "Repeat the dependency census for every direct Naga and WGPU use and record the exact module that owns private WGSL evidence.",
        "Migrate the G4C1 resource-private DeviceHealth into the one WgpuContextState-owned WgpuDeviceHealth without changing accepted G4C1 public failure semantics; delete the resource-private health owner and duplicate observer-install path.",
        "Route existing G4C1 resource backend creation and CurrentRenderDeviceQueue through the single WgpuErrorAttributionGate before G4C2 can use scoped creation, so unrelated current WGPU operations cannot be captured by another task's G4C2 error scopes.",
        "Refactor the current high-level render integration so its G4C1/G4C2 realization phase completes before the raw CurrentRenderDeviceQueue loan begins. The split is migration ordering only: it does not move pipeline realization into G4C2 or command encoding/submission into G4C2.",
        "Migrate explicit program/interface/layout/bind-group realization through the async G4C2 owner while retaining filesystem/watch/reload/LKG policy in Runenwerk and semantic shader meaning in RunenRender or other consumers.",
        "Do not introduce blocking, executor, or event-loop policy in RunenGPU. If current synchronous Runenwerk code must drive a G4C2 future, locate that choice at the narrowest audited Runenwerk product/integration boundary before raw-loan acquisition and source-guard it as non-framework policy.",
        "Migrate every GpuRuntimeBindingResource::Sampler consumer through its accepted GpuSamplerHandle and G4C1 sampler realization; delete renderer sampler placeholders/creation paths replaced by that authority and do not create an inline G4C2 sampler exception.",
        "Migrate CurrentRenderResourceBridge terminals that G4C2 owns to typed G4C2 bind-group realization, delete that predecessor bridge, and record the only residual resource terminals that the successor may retain.",
